# Files Shopify CLI skips on theme push, pull and dev, as paths from the theme root. An entry is a simple name, a
# wildcard or a /regular expression/ (shopify.dev "Shopify CLI for themes"). Only the theme folders belong on a
# store; the repo's tooling and docs stay local (`shopify theme package` zips the theme folders only).
# CLI 4.9 warns "Directory pattern may be misleading" for any entry that ends in "/" without a "*". Every regular
# expression ends in "/", so the folder rule ends in .* ("anything below the folder") and draws no warning.
/^(docs|scripts|tests|dist|\.harness|\.github|node_modules)\/.*/
